Hi Rachit! We rebuilt the pipeline on the `jia` branch (one plain package, a README per part, ~180 tests). It hasn't
run end to end on a real model yet, and anton is yours. Could you run it?

SETUP, ONCE

    git fetch origin && git checkout jia
    # keep your existing deploy/server/local.env: same variable names as yours
    # add HF_TOKEN=... to it if your Hugging Face account needs it for the Mistral models
    ./panther build          # the image: CUDA 12.9, llama.cpp at the pinned commit, our env from uv.lock

FIRST RUN, THE SMALLEST CONTEST

    ./panther run 1.5b@1     # fetch container (network: data + model), then run container (GPU, no network)
    ./panther logs 1.5b@1    # follow it
    ./panther stop 1.5b@1    # if it needs stopping

If it stops for any reason (./panther stop, a crash, a reboot), just run ./panther run 1.5b@1 again: it continues
where it stopped. The costliest place to stop is while the type copies are being built.

WHAT IT DOES, IN ORDER

1. Builds the dataset from pinned sources (four disjoint sets: GA, winner, distill, verdict).
2. Downloads the model and makes 13 GPTQ type copies.
3. Picks the preset on the winner set.
4. Runs the genetic search on the GA set.
5. Distills the 3 finalists, then picks the winner on the winner set.
6. Gives a verdict against the preset on the verdict set: WIN / TIE / LOSE with a 95 % interval.

The verdict prints at the end. Everything is saved under data/contests/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct@1/ (preset.json,
search.json, winner.json, verdict.json, winner.gguf).

GOOD TO KNOW

- Disk: ~13 GB for the 1.5B. The big models need ~190 GB each (the download is kept, the type copies are
  deletable), so one big model at a time on 500 GB.
- QAT is off by default. ./panther run 1.5b@1 --qat 1024 adds your Block-AP (ported, with all four of your fixes).
  Its disk cache is large: ~52 GB for the 1.5B at 1,024 samples, much more for the big models.
- This is the first real run, so something may break. Every step fails loudly with a traceback in the log. Whenever
  it stops, please paste us the last ~50 lines of ./panther logs 1.5b@1. We fix it, you run the same command again,
  and it continues where it stopped.
- If 1.5b@1 gets through, next would be 7b@3.

IF YOU (OR YOUR CLAUDE) WANT TO REUSE WHAT IS ALREADY DOWNLOADED ON ANTON

Reuse raw downloads only, never anything made from them:

- Datasets: nothing to do. Our containers use the same Hugging Face cache as yours (HF_HOME=/work/data/cache/hf
  under the same data folder) and the same pinned revisions, so the dataset build reads them from the cache.
- Model weights: our run keeps the downloaded Hugging Face weights in data/models/<model>/hf/ (GPTQ, the tokenizer,
  distillation and QAT read them), so it downloads them once (3 GB for the 1.5B) unless they are already in the
  cache. You may link your existing 16-bit GGUF to save the conversion, but only if it was converted at the
  llama.cpp commit in configs/models.yaml:
      ln -s ../../store/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct-BF16.gguf data/models/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct/original.gguf
- Do NOT reuse or link: imatrix files, type copies, preset files, KL references (.kld), the old data/splits/, or
  any records. They were made under the old definitions (14 types, no output-layer importance data, other
  calibration text, another distillation loss). Our pipeline would treat them as done, skip remaking them, and the
  results would be silently wrong.
- Do not change the pipeline's code to point at the old layout: the paths are part of how each step knows it is
  done.

